>> title: Mushroom Risotto
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: rice, mushrooms, italian, stovetop
>> counters: Pizzeria
>> aka: risotto ai funghi, risotto ai porcini
>> servings: 4
>> time: 45 min
>> slack: narrow — al dente is the last thing to happen and it does not wait; overshoot it and you have porridge, which is a different dish

>> step: brown 10 min
Brown @cremini mushrooms{12%oz}(340 g; sliced) with @thyme{1%tsp}(fresh leaves, chopped) in @olive oil{2%Tbs} in a #skillet{} for ~{10%min}.

>> step: sweat 4 min
Sweat @shallot{1%large}(minced) in @unsalted butter{2%Tbs} in a #wide saucepan{} for ~{4%min}.

>> step: toast 2 min, deglaze
Toast @&(~1)shallot{} with @Arborio rice{1 1/2%cups}(300 g) for ~{2%min}, then deglaze with @dry white wine{1/2%cup}(120 mL).

>> step: ladle in, stir 18 min
Add @chicken stock{6%cups}(1.4 L; kept hot) to @&(~1)rice{} a ladleful at a time, stirring, until the grains are al dente, ~{18%min}.

>> step: beat in off the heat
Beat @&(~4)mushrooms{}, @grated Parmesan{3/4%cup}(65 g), @cold unsalted butter{2%Tbs}, and @kosher salt{1%tsp} into @&(~1)risotto{} off the heat.
